** Other Useful Protocols 1.4 **
GRE - The tunnel between two endpoints
	No built in encryption
IKE - Agree on encryption/decryption keys without sending the key across the network by building the Security Association
	Phase 1 - Use DH to craete a shared key on udp/500
		ISAKMP - Internet Security Association and Key Management Protocol
	Phase 2 - Coordinate ciphers and key sizes
		Negotiate an inbound and outbound SA for IPsec
Transport Mode and Tunnel Mode
	Original packet -> IP Header | Data
	Transport mode -> IP Header | IPsec Headers | Data | IPsec Trailers
	Tunnel mode -> New IP Header | IPsec Headers | IP Header | Data | IPsec Trailers
AH - Hash of the packet and a shared key
		MD5, SHA-1, or SHA-2 for the hash
		Adds the AH to the header packet
		New IP Header | AH Header | IP Header | Data
ESP - Encrypts the packet
	MD5, SHA-1, or SHA-2 for the hash
	3DES or AES for encryption
	Adds a header, a trailer, and an integrity check value
	New IP Header | ESP Header | IP Header | Data | ESP Trailer | Integrity Check Value

