** Calculating IPv4 Subnets and Hosts 1.7 **
VLSM
Number of subnets = 2^subnet bits
Hosts per subnet = 2^ host bits - 2
IP address: 10.1.1.0/24
	Class: A
	Network bits: 8
	Subnet bits: 16
	Total subnets: 65536
	Hosts per subnet: 254
IP address: 192.168.11.0/26
	Class = C
	Network bits: 24
	Subnet bits: 2
	Total subnets: 4
	Hosts per subnet: 62	
IP address: 172.16.55.0/21
	Class: B
	Network bits: 16
	Subnet bits: 5
	Total subnets: 32
	Hosts per subnet: 2046

